---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// The sign-in paragraph below describes the wallet, so it renders only in a
// build where the wallet is switched on (wallet-config.ts's flag; ADR 0008,
// "Switch it on"). With it off, no visitor is offered sign-in at all.
const walletEnabled = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_WALLET_ENABLED === 'true';
---

<BaseLayout title="What we log, and why — Dontdropthatpromo">
  <h1>What we log, and why</h1>
  <p>
    Every screen in this app fires a real event at a hosted database, so there's an actual
    aggregate to look at, not a simulated one. Here's exactly what that means, event family by
    event family:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>A random ID for this browser</strong>, generated the first time you do anything here
      and stored only in this browser. It isn't your name, email, or anything that identifies you —
      it's a made-up number that lets us tell "one visitor came back" from "two different
      visitors," nothing more.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Which city you're browsing, and when you switch</strong> — <code>location_selected</code>,
      fired only the first time you pick a city or when you pick a different one than the city
      already remembered for this browser, never on every visit.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Which screens you visit and when</strong> — the home feed (<code>home_viewed</code>),
      a restaurant's menu (<code>restaurant_opened</code>), your cart (<code>cart_viewed</code>),
      checkout (<code>checkout_viewed</code>), and the tracker, including every time you come back
      to check on an order (<code>tracker_viewed</code>).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The flash-deal sheet that sometimes opens on the home feed</strong> — <code>flash_sheet_shown</code>
      (which restaurants and what discount were randomly drawn
      for you this browsing session; not recorded at the moment, while the sheet's larger draw of five or six
      restaurants is brought into the log) and <code>flash_sheet_closed</code> (whether you tapped one of
      the two restaurants, dismissed the sheet, or let its countdown run out). That draw is random,
      done in this browser, and tied to this one session — it isn't a promise the same deal is
      available to anyone else, or to you again later.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The choices you make at checkout</strong> — your drop-off preset (Home, Office, or
      Front desk), your delivery instructions, whether you want utensils, and which real voucher or
      vouchers, if any, you applied (<code>order_placed</code>). There is no name, address, phone
      number, email, or payment field anywhere in this app for us to log, because we never ask for
      one, and no free-text field anywhere in this app, ever.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Whether your order actually arrives, and how you rated it</strong> — <code>order_delivered</code>,
      the first time the tracker computes your order as delivered, and <code>rating_submitted</code>,
      the star count and any preset tags (never free text) you choose
      when you submit a rating.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p data-testid="driver-avatar-credit">
    Driver avatars: Avataaars by Pablo Stanley, via DiceBear (MIT).
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What we don't log:</strong> anything that identifies you as a real person, in the events
    above. No card, no address, no cross-site tracking cookie, and no free-text field anywhere in
    this app for any of the above, ever — because the choices above are the only ones this app
    actually asks you to make.
  </p>
  {walletEnabled && (
  <p>
    <strong>If you sign in to place an order:</strong> Google or Apple shares an email address with
    us, which Supabase Auth holds to keep your play-money wallet tied to your account. Your balance
    is stored per account in our database — never in the events above, and never joined to the
    random browser ID. It's still play money: no payment is ever taken.
  </p>
  )}
  <div class="demo-disclosure" data-testid="about-disclosure">
    <span
      ><svg
        class="icon-info"
        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
        fill="none"
        stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="2"
        aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9.5"></circle><line x1="12" y1="11" x2="12" y2="16.5"
        ></line><circle cx="12" cy="7.5" r="1.2" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"></circle></svg
      ></span
    >
    <span>
      <strong>One more thing, in the interest of actually being honest about it:</strong> to stop spam
      from overwhelming this free database, every write is checked against a short-term limit keyed to
      a scrambled (one-way hashed) version of your IP address. That scrambled value is kept for <strong>up to one hour</strong>,
      only to enforce that limit, and it never appears next to anything
      you did here — it isn't stored in the same place as the events above and can't be joined back to
      them. We're naming it here because it's still something your visit causes this site to process,
      even though it never becomes part of the dataset you can query.
    </span>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
